rators preserve M_R and x,y,h preserve M.\",\"new\":\"N002 says all these operators preserve both M and M_R, and gives the induced Chevalley action after tensoring. In particular the induced x,y,h satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y and [x,y]=h on V(K), because tensor extension preserves sums and compositions of lattice endomorphisms.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"family I→ℂ\",\"scope\":\"independence test\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary complex coefficients c=(c_i)_{i∈I} to test linear independence.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\",\"scope\":\"independence test\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary j∈I to isolate its coefficient in a putative relation.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"To check independence, take any relation ∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i=0 with complex coefficients and any j∈I; apply\",\"new\":\"To check independence, fix arbitrary c:I→ℂ and j∈I, and temporarily assume L2: ∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i=0. Apply\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"Thus the whole family is linearly independent.\",\"new\":\"Since j was arbitrary every coefficient is zero. Discharging L2 and quantifying over c proves that the whole family is linearly independent.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/objects/-\",\"value\":\"c\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/objects/-\",\"value\":\"j\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/rules/-\",\"value\":\"implication_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"old\":\"these coefficients are nonzero scalars for i∈I.\",\"new\":\"these eigenvalue-difference factors are nonzero scalars for i∈I.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/logic/rules/-\",\"value\":\"negation_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/rules/-\",\"value\":\"negation_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/rules/-\",\"value\":\"implication_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"If J were zero every projection\",\"new\":\"Temporarily assume L1: J={0}. Then every projection\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"This contradicts its complex span V and n>0 from N001.\",\"new\":\"This contradicts its complex span V and n>0 from N001. Discharge L1 to conclude J≠{0}.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L1\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L1\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"rational line assertion\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary a∈J; the condition a≠0 is the local antecedent L2 in S005.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"z\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"rational line assertion\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary z∈J to prove the rational-line assertion for every element.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/text\",\"value\":\"Fix arbitrary a,z∈J and temporarily assume L2: a≠0. Injectivity of μ in F002 gives 1⊗a≠0, since its image is a. The singleton family consisting of 1⊗a is linearly independent over ℚ: a scalar annihilating a nonzero vector in a vector space over a field is zero. Apply M003 with A=ℚ, ambient space T, the singleton index type and this singleton family. F004 gives the required dimension 1, so 1⊗z=q(1⊗a) for some q∈ℚ. Applying μ proves z=qa for that q. Discharge L2 and quantify over a,z: for every nonzero a∈J every element of J is a rational multiple of a. Together with F001–F004 this proves the stated coordinate decomposition, injectivity, and rational rank-one conclusion.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/objects/-\",\"value\":\"a\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/objects/-\",\"value\":\"z\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"Apply this to all the finitely many q_j, writing q_j=p^{ν_j}u_j with ν_j∈ℤ and u_j∈R×. The nonempty finite list of integer exponents has a minimum ν and an index j_0 attaining it.\",\"new\":\"Apply this to all the finitely many nonzero rational coefficients of g relative to a. For each there is an integer exponent and a unit of R; the nonempty finite list of exponents has a minimum and an index attaining it. These are precisely the existential data in F002.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/uses/-\",\"value\":\"H003\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"Its member β_0 is nonzero since 0∈I and basis vectors are independent;\",\"new\":\"H003 gives 0∈I. Its member β_0 is nonzero since basis vectors are independent;\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/produces/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"V(K)≠{0}.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"V(K)\"],\"assumptions\":[]}},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"together with the zero case this proves W={0} or W=V(K) under L1.\",\"new\":\"together with the zero case this proves W={0} or W=V(K) under L1. Discharge L1 into the antecedent to obtain F002.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/2/text\",\"old\":\"and S001 already proved V(K)≠0.\",\"new\":\"and F003 proves V(K)≠0.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/2/uses_local/-\",\"value\":\"F003\"}]}}","status":"completed"}}

