op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/14/statement\",\"old\":\"and M_R is free of rank n over R. Under this embedding M_R is stable under all X_r,Y_r (r≥0).\",\"new\":\"and M_R has an R-basis indexed by I, of rank n. Every X_r,Y_r (r≥0) preserves M and, under this embedding, also preserves M_R.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/spec/definitions/12/definition\",\"value\":\"V(K)=M⊗_ℤ K. Every ℤ-linear operator on M acts by its tensor extension on V(K). The same symbols x,y,h,X_r,Y_r denote the tensor-induced actions of their restrictions to M once their preservation of M has been proved; this notation asserts no such preservation by itself.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/spec/definitions/12/depends_on\",\"value\":[\"D003\",\"D004\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/spec/definitions/12/objects\",\"value\":[\"M\",\"K\",\"x\",\"y\",\"h\",\"X\",\"Y\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/definitions/12/binders/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"r\",\"type\":\"nonnegative integer\"}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/definitions/12/objects/-\",\"value\":\"r\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/propositions/17/statement\",\"old\":\"On β the actions x,y,h and all divided powers X_r,Y_r have the following integer matrices reduced to K:\",\"new\":\"The operators x,y,h and X_r,Y_r here are the tensor-induced lattice operators. The actions of x,y,h give the induced representation of the Chevalley ℤ-form tensored with K, and satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y, [x,y]=h on V(K). On β they and all the divided powers have the following integer matrices reduced to K:\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/4/argument/3/text\",\"old\":\"N002 says the operators preserve M_R and x,y,h preserve M.\",\"new\":\"N002 says all these operators preserve both M and M_R, and gives the induced Chevalley action after tensoring. In particular the induced x,y,h satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=-2y and [x,y]=h on V(K), because tensor extension preserves sums and compositions of lattice endomorphisms.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"c\",\"type\":\"family I→ℂ\",\"scope\":\"independence test\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary complex coefficients c=(c_i)_{i∈I} to test linear independence.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"j\",\"type\":\"element of I\",\"scope\":\"independence test\",\"start\":\"S002\",\"end\":\"S002\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary j∈I to isolate its coefficient in a putative relation.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"I\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"To check independence, take any relation ∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i=0 with complex coefficients and any j∈I; apply\",\"new\":\"To check independence, fix arbitrary c:I→ℂ and j∈I, and temporarily assume L2: ∑_{i∈I}c_i e_i=0. Apply\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"Thus the whole family is linearly independent.\",\"new\":\"Since j was arbitrary every coefficient is zero. Discharging L2 and quantifying over c proves that the whole family is linearly independent.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/objects/-\",\"value\":\"c\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/objects/-\",\"value\":\"j\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/rules/-\",\"value\":\"implication_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"old\":\"these coefficients are nonzero scalars for i∈I.\",\"new\":\"these eigenvalue-difference factors are nonzero scalars for i∈I.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/spec/logic/rules/-\",\"value\":\"negation_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/rules/-\",\"value\":\"negation_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/rules/-\",\"value\":\"implication_introduction\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"If J were zero every projection\",\"new\":\"Temporarily assume L1: J={0}. Then every projection\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"This contradicts its complex span V and n>0 from N001.\",\"new\":\"This contradicts its complex span V and n>0 from N001. Discharge L1 to conclude J≠{0}.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L1\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/0/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L1\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"a\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"rational line assertion\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary a∈J; the condition a≠0 is the local antecedent L2 in S005.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/locals/-\",\"value\":{\"symbol\":\"z\",\"type\":\"element of J\",\"scope\":\"rational line assertion\",\"start\":\"S005\",\"end\":\"S005\",\"kind\":\"arbitrary\",\"declaration\":\"Fix arbitrary z∈J to prove the rational-line assertion for every element.\",\"from_inputs\":[],\"from_local\":[],\"objects\":[\"J\"]}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/text\",\"value\":\"Fix arbitrary a,z∈J and temporarily assume L2: a≠0. Injectivity of μ in F002 gives 1⊗a≠0, since its image is a. The singleton family consisting of 1⊗a is linearly independent over ℚ: a scalar annihilating a nonzero vector in a vector space over a field is zero. Apply M003 with A=ℚ, ambient space T, the singleton index type and this singleton family. F004 gives the required dimension 1, so 1⊗z=q(1⊗a) for some q∈ℚ. Applying μ proves z=qa for that q. Discharge L2 and quantify over a,z: for every nonzero a∈J every element of J is a rational multiple of a. Together with F001–F004 this proves the stated coordinate decomposition, injectivity, and rational rank-one conclusion.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/introduces\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/discharges\",\"value\":[\"L2\"]},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/objects/-\",\"value\":\"a\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/2/argument/4/objects/-\",\"value\":\"z\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/3/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"Apply this to all the finitely many q_j, writing q_j=p^{ν_j}u_j with ν_j∈ℤ and u_j∈R×. The nonempty finite list of integer exponents has a minimum ν and an index j_0 attaining it.\",\"new\":\"Apply this to all the finitely many nonzero rational coefficients of g relative to a. For each there is an integer exponent and a unit of R; the nonempty finite list of exponents has a minimum and an index attaining it. These are precisely the existential data in F002.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/uses/-\",\"value\":\"H003\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/text\",\"old\":\"Its member β_0 is nonzero since 0∈I and basis vectors are independent;\",\"new\":\"H003 gives 0∈I. Its member β_0 is nonzero since basis vectors are independent;\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/0/produces/-\",\"value\":{\"id\":\"F003\",\"statement\":\"V(K)≠{0}.\",\"binders\":[],\"objects\":[\"V(K)\"],\"assumptions\":[]}},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/1/text\",\"old\":\"together with the zero case this proves W={0} or W=V(K) under L1.\",\"new\":\"together with the zero case this proves W={0} or W=V(K) under L1. Discharge L1 into the antecedent to obtain F002.\"},{\"op\":\"replace_text\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/2/text\",\"old\":\"and S001 already proved V(K)≠0.\",\"new\":\"and F003 proves V(K)≠0.\"},{\"op\":\"add\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/5/argument/2/uses_local/-\",\"value\":\"F003\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"resolutions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","location","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"output_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","note"],"additionalProperties":false}},"inference_notes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"dependency_and_local_assumption_check":{"type":"string"},"source_application_check":{"type":"string"},"declaration_check":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","dependency_and_local_assumption_check","source_application_check","declaration_check"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["candidate","readiness","open_issues","original_context_note","output_notes","inference_notes"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"af8af185-2464-4eb3-a3bf-4735ea6ee764","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"high"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":129773,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4248,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1966},"total_tokens":134021,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6c419ac819190ab2b31fa78ad15":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6d2b08881918c36b21b7617124b":{"input_tokens":30,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6ddc4cc8191b95a87a58ea9498c":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6e209148191a66397f3e6e045ef":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6e63eb48191aab20003f063f8a8":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6eb2c9c819184e5b5874506cbc9":{"input_tokens":33,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0260ceffca0ed12f016adef6f0a34c81918e342e89f9316